DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ffeexxeeccvvee() performs the same task as eexxeeccvvee(2), with the difference that
       the  file to be executed is specified via a file descriptor, _f_d, rather
       than via a pathname.  The file descriptor _f_d must be  opened  read‐only
       (OO__RRDDOONNLLYY)  or with the OO__PPAATTHH flag and the caller must have permission
       to execute the file that it refers to.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       A successful call to ffeexxeeccvvee() never returns.  On error,  the  function
       does  return,  with  a result value of -1, and _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate
       the error.

